&Q000358

{1 = 1-12}
1.	Men used to eat grass with their mouths like sheep. 
2.	In those times, they did not know grain, barley or flax. 
3.	@wDN{An} brought these down from the interior of heaven. 
4.	@wDN{Enlil} lifted his gaze around as a stag lifts its horns when climbing the terraced …… hills. 
5.	He looked southwards and saw the wide sea; 
6.	he looked northwards and saw the mountain of aromatic cedars. 
7.	@wDN{Enlil} piled up the barley, gave it to the mountain. 
8.	He piled up the bounty of the Land, gave the @fsux{innuḫa} barley to the mountain. 
9.	He closed off access to the wide-open hill. 
10.	He …… its lock, 
11.	which heaven and earth shut fast (?), 
12.	its bolt, which ……. 

{13 = 13-20}
13.	Then @wDN{Ninazu} ……, and said to his brother @wDN{Ninmada}: 
14.	@q[Ninazu,Ninmada]{“Let us go to the mountain, 
15.	to the mountain where barley and flax grow; 
16.	…… the rolling river, 
17.	where the water wells up from the earth. 
18.	Let us fetch the barley down from its mountain, 
19.	let us introduce the @fsux{innuḫa} barley into @wGN{Sumer}. 
20.	Let us make barley known in @wGN{Sumer}, which knows no barley.”} 

{21 = 21-27}
21.	@wDN{Ninmada}, the worshipper of @wDN{An}, replied to him: 
22.	@q[Ninmada,Ninazu]{“Since our father has not given the command, 
23.	since @wDN{Enlil} has not given the command, 
24.	how can we go there to the mountain? 
25.	How can we bring down the barley from its mountain? 
26.	How can we introduce the @fsux{innuḫa} grain into @wGN{Sumer}? 
27.	How can we make barley known in @wGN{Sumer}, which knows no barley?”} 

{28 = 28-31}
28.	@q{“Come, let us go to @wDN{Utu} of heaven, who as he lies there, 
29.	as he lies there, sleeps a sound sleep, to the hero, 
30.	the son of @wDN{Ningal}, who as he lies there sleeps a sound sleep.”} 
31.	He raised his hands towards @wDN{Utu} of the seventy doors (?). 

{32 = 32}
32.	@wDN{Utu} …… table (?) ……. 
